                  "datavalue": {
                    "value": {
                      "text": "Occurents have temporal parts and thus cannot be present at a time-boundary. Time belongs to them, because they happen in time and the time of the occurent is built into it. The relation between an occurent and a chronoid is determined by the projection relation. Occurents are also called generalized processes in the GFO.",
